[subsection {Version 0.9.4.23}]

[list_begin itemized]

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: [method getStringWidth] extended with optional
keyword arguments [option -font] and [option -size] (0.9.4.23+).
Text width can now be measured without a prior [method setFont] call.
CIDFont metrics are supported. Legacy positional call unchanged.

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: [method inPage] added. Returns [const 1] if a
page is currently open, [const 0] otherwise.

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: [method currentPage] added. Returns the current
page number (1-based, [const 0] before first [method startPage]).
[method pageCount] added -- returns the number of completed pages.

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: [method drawTextBox] gains [option -newyvar]
option. The named variable receives the Y position after the last rendered
line in the current unit. Allows flowing text without manual recalculation.

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: Annotation methods added (ISO 32000 SS12.5):
[method addAnnotNote], [method addAnnotFreeText],
[method addAnnotHighlight], [method addAnnotUnderline],
[method addAnnotStrikeOut], [method addAnnotStamp], [method addAnnotLine].

[item] [file src/cat.tcl]: [cmd ::pdf4tcl::exportForms] added.
Exports form field data from a filled PDF as FDF (ISO 32000 SS12.7.7)
or XFDF (SS12.7.8). Returns the number of exported fields.

[item] [file src/options.tcl]: [option {-pdfa 3b}] added as valid value.
PDF/A-3b allows embedded files with associated file relationships.

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: [method addEmbeddedFile] now tracks FileSpec OIDs
for the document-level [const /AF] array when [option {-pdfa 3b}] is active.
The [const /AF] array in the Catalog associates embedded files with the
document as a whole (ISO 19005-3 SS6.2.11.4).

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: [method addLayer] / [method beginLayer]:
[const /AS] array added to the OCG [const /D] dictionary when
[option {-pdfa 2b}] or [option {-pdfa 3b}] is active (ISO 19005-2 SS6.2.10).
Defines layer state for Print and View events. Standard PDFs and
PDF/A-1b are not affected.

[item] [file tests/new-0.9.4.23-annot.test]: 20 new tests for
annotation methods ([method addAnnotNote], [method addAnnotFreeText],
[method addAnnotHighlight], [method addAnnotUnderline],
[method addAnnotStrikeOut], [method addAnnotStamp], [method addAnnotLine]).

[item] [file tests/new-0.9.4.23.test]: 23 new tests --
[option {-pdfa 3b}] validation (3), [const /AF] array (4),
[const /AS] array (5), [method getStringWidth] with [option -font]/[option -size] (3),
[method inPage] / [method currentPage] / [method pageCount] (5),
[method drawTextBox] [option -newyvar] (2), [cmd ::pdf4tcl::exportForms] (5).

[list_end]

[subsection {Version 0.9.4.22}]

[list_begin itemized]

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: PDF/A-2b now writes a cross-reference stream
([method _WriteXrefStream]) instead of a classic xref table.
Required by ISO 19005-2 SS6.1.4. PDF/A-1b continues to use the classic
table (XRef streams forbidden by ISO 19005-1 SS6.1.3).
Classic xref table extracted into [method _WriteXrefTable].

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: PDF version set to 1.7 for [option {-pdfa 2b}]
(ISO 19005-2 SS4.1 requires PDF 1.7 as base format).
PDF/A-1b and standard PDFs remain at PDF 1.4.

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: [method setAlpha] with a value less than 1.0
under [option {-pdfa 1b}] appends a warning to [var ::pdf4tcl::warnings]
(transparency forbidden by ISO 19005-1 SS6.1.3).
No exception is raised -- the PDF is generated regardless.

[item] [file src/prologue.tcl]: [var ::pdf4tcl::warnings] list added.
Accumulates non-fatal compliance warnings. Check after document creation;
reset with [cmd {set ::pdf4tcl::warnings {}}].

[item] [file src/encrypt.tcl]: MD5 backend chain added ([method _InitMD5Backend],
[method _MD5], [method _MD5Init], [method _MD5Update], [method _MD5Final],
[method _MD5PureTcl]).
Priority: Tcllib md5 -> openssl -> pure-Tcl implementation (RFC 1321).
AES-128 encryption now works on FIPS systems without Tcllib.

[item] [file tests/new-0.9.4.22.test]: 17 new tests --
XRef-Stream (7), PDF version (3), setAlpha warning (2), MD5 pure-Tcl (5).

[item] [file demo/demo-pdfa.tcl]: New page 4 documenting XRef-Stream
structure, PDF/A-2b implementation, and 0.9.4.22 fixes.
PDF version on page 1 now dynamically reflects actual document version.

[item] [file demo/demo-alpha.tcl]: New section 8 showing the
[option {-pdfa 1b}] + [method setAlpha] warning mechanism.

[list_end]

[subsection {Version 0.9.4.21}]

[list_begin itemized]

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: ICC profile stream compressed with
[const FlateDecode] when [option -compress] is active.
Previously written as raw uncompressed stream.
Saves approximately 2 KB per PDF/A document.

[item] [file src/main.tcl]: New public methods [method addLayer],
[method beginLayer], [method endLayer] implement Optional Content Groups
(OCG / Layers, ISO 32000 SS8.11).
Supports debug grids, letterhead variants, watermarks.
Layer visibility controlled by [option -visible] (default: 1).

